{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-07T09:56:24.757Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-CALLBACK-GAS-01","attempt":1,"title":"GAP-008: how much gas does the follow-up step of a payout really burn, per member?","tier":"testnet","hypothesis":"Written before the run. The follow-up step (on_settlement_payout) applies each member's deduction and clears the settling mark. Its cost is a base plus a per-member part. Prediction: the base is under 10 TGas and the per-member part is under 1 TGas, so the sizing 25 TGas + 1 TGas per member (capped at 100) is enough for the 50-member maximum (about 75 TGas). The contract deployed at the time of the run may give it a flat 25 TGas; if the measured cost extrapolated to 50 members exceeds the allotment in force, that is the GAP-008 risk, shown. Fails if the follow-up step fails to run or settle, or if the measured per-member cost is 1 TGas or more (the sizing would then be too small).","limits":["Measures gas from the settlement's own receipts on testnet for 4 and N members and extrapolates linearly to 50; it does not run 50 members.","It cannot make a real callback run out of gas, so the recovery path itself is shown by unit tests, not live.","One operator controls every account and the host is local."],"requires":["near-key","network"],"chain_prev":"e84b070b1dfe5fe891939d621c16e3fa96aa851d83b5dffc433f8a056fe6d700","chain_hash":"8be84e998dcd0cd546926532b156c1a05f2584c58b590f9b5db4b3a403597c96"}
